NAME
       expr - evaluate an expression

SYNOPSIS
       expr EXPRESSION

DESCRIPTION
       Evaluates an arithmetic or string expression and prints the
       result. Operators and operands are separate arguments, so they
       must be spaced apart and multiplication escaped from globbing.

EXAMPLES
       expr 6 + 7
       expr 6 '*' 7

SEE ALSO
       test(1), calc(1), csh(1)
